==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{term|aldr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*aldrą}}, whence also Old English {{term|ealdor|lang=ang}}, Old High German {{term|altar|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*al-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₂el-||to grow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈaltʊɹ]|lang=fo}}
*: {{rhymes|altʊɹ|lang=fo}}

===Noun===
{{fo-noun|m|aldurs|aldrar}}

# [[age]]
# age, [[seniority]]
# [[time]], [[era]]

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-noun-m19|ald|r}}

====Synonyms====
* [[ævi]], [[æviskeið]], [[lívstíð]]
* [[elli]], [[aldurdómur]]
* [[tíð]], [[tíðarskeið]]

===Anagrams===
* {{l|fo|dalur}}

